# Graphify: CODE-ONLY. Files graphify classifies as doc/paper/image get an LLM semantic pass in a full
# `graphify .` but a raw structural pass in `graphify update .` (the commit hook) -> the hook's graph
# would diverge from a manual build. Excluding them keeps both identical and the auto-rebuild reliable.
# (Doc/markdown knowledge lives in the semantic index, not the code graph.)
*.md
*.mdx
*.qmd
*.rst
*.txt
*.html
*.yaml
*.yml
*.pdf
*.png
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.gif
*.svg
*.webp
# editor/vault noise graphify pulls in (it doesn't honor .gitignore except as a fallback)
.obsidian/
.claude/
graphify-out/